              'https://deadline.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/01/thesocialnetwork-dl.pdf',
              "<b>Director's eye: stage the turn, do not explain it.</b> Fincher can let performance, cutting rhythm, eyelines and the "
              "room's distance register a power shift. In your draft, give the actor an action and a prop or spatial choice that the "
              'camera can read. “He feels rejected” is not a scene direction; “he pockets the apology card” is filmable behaviour.',
